From d029bee07883280b52ddb3290798e378c51002ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:31:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Say that measurements are not the health card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Asked "aké som mal operácie v minulosti", the assistant answered that the
database holds only measurements and family history — correct — and then, asked
whether it could not see the scanned card, said yes, it sees everything, and
listed 246 records from a source called "ocr" as proof. Both halves came from
the same gap: the context named the source but never said what it contains.

It contains numbers. The extractor pulls measurable values out of a scanned
report and everything around them — diagnoses, operations, medication, the
doctor's conclusion — was discarded before it reached the database. So a
question that can only be answered from the report's prose has no source at all,
and a source line reading "ocr: 246 meraní" reads to the model like the card
itself.

The document section now says this explicitly when nothing is indexed: no
document text is stored, the ocr rows are numbers only, and re-uploading the
document is what makes its text available. The system prompt gains the matching
rule, so the model stops treating measurements as evidence that it can read the
card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
